    "body": "I think this should use https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#internal-pause-steps, but I guess that setting the \"autoplay on demand flag\" to false would prevent autoplay the next time the video intersects the viewport? It'd be fine to just say \"invoke the internal pause steps and set the autoplay on demand flag to false\" instead.\r\n\r\nI think it would be good to point out that the steps for playing and pausing can be triggered many times. Because this inside an algorithm, my default assumption would be that one never jumps to an earlier step implicitly.",
